,"englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"623a40dfc6932e2d71583a3b2baa12611d345b34fe35f62da818e73339c40400","compact":"10f7205b9b2c6b61335ab008426efe7e47aa7c516a80572c448ed8d5bddbd986","nasal":"35554cbf974c83714c568091c572c0339df21cd775e0b1cb8d3b0f6dc5f646dc"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-42-7","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":42,"verse":7,"english":"He pierced that lord of monkey's face with half-moon (shaped) arrows, his head with one having its head made like a hook and his arms with ten nārācas. (Iron arrows).","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.879,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-44-7"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5042007","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ea02f7fb985dad47eeeec5b7893963c1b46e65a7d57b70b801cfa730d7733349","compact":"f1592c8d574de436676555156fd1b529762e0896aea30e9fa824fe637abe1c73","nasal":"b055ee934939ba0ffed336afde7d3ddfac6b2fa85e12849da21f211caf9c5a72"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-42-8","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":42,"verse":8,"english":"And pierced by the arrows, his coppery face looked beautiful like a blown autumnal red lotus shot at by the solar rays.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.844,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-44-8"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5042008","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ad46afe12736222b334ab6dd90703450551cf3bf7fee4984260661b269b055d9","compact":"de0a755679e2649eb208be13664b97345b29bfeb710e4f515d0ba727923857cf","nasal":"4aec368143faaae08c3d5435aadf74f1c12277df8cd976dee1e47d67ca30fb05"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-42-9","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":42,"verse":9,"english":"And his naturally red countenance being painted with blood, looked lovely like a majestic red lotus in the sky, washed with the honey of the red Asoka. Wounded by the shafts, the redoubted grew enraged. And he espied a huge and gigantic crag beside him. Thereat, at once uprooting it, that one endowed with celerity and strength hurled it (at his foe).","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-44-9"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5042009","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b9e49cbe5ce89a77d676cbd5372cbe1dbecd06a55d01e2539b9787c06814c0cd","compact":"311123dee238bf27f7993be43682e54cbbe9ef5eb0b31e929b42bb29bcc12b0b","nasal":"311123dee238bf27f7993be43682e54cbbe9ef5eb0b31e929b42bb29bcc12b0b"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-42-10","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":42,"verse":10,"english":"And his naturally red countenance being painted with blood, looked lovely like a majestic red lotus in the sky, washed with the honey of the red Asoka. Wounded by the shafts, the redoubted grew enraged. And he espied a huge and gigantic crag beside him. Thereat, at once uprooting it, that one endowed with celerity and strength hurled it (at his foe). And the enraged Rākṣasa opposed it by ten shafts. Witnessing his action rendered fruitless, the energetic Hanumān of terrific prowess, uprooting a large Sāla, began to whirl it in the air).","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.516,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-44-9","DUTT-5-44-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5042010","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"76833f048c44f1cd78cce8b11bc3eea9266beec78c9834e09f2c73a4bd610524","compact":"99fcb575ecf5a4317bf56af40538b68b51add9db8b965b3d8d16e7a1a5397860","nasal":"99fcb575ecf5a4317bf56af40538b68b51add9db8b965b3d8d16e7a1a5397860"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-42-11","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":42,"verse":11,"english":"And the enraged Rākṣasa opposed it by ten shafts. Witnessing his action rendered fruitless, the energetic Hanumān of terrific prowess, uprooting a large Sāla, began to whirl it in the air).","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-44-10"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5042011","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"8b18ed8527bd0808d60d343d24c44543ce81d1a5faedf6b084c3090d81fb7d67","compact":"2ae10de19df997f17f0cc7e3a24867af49f5b402ea3be7d641c63b2eefe4c059","nasal":"622109dbd51d07bbcacdeb7c6eaf74a305cfd5a531206459108971420dafa5f8"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-42-12","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":42,"verse":12,"english":"Seeing the exceedingly strong monkey whirling the Sāla tree, the highly powerful Jambumālī dischanged a many shafts.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-44-11"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5042012","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"289cb4e1b7efcbf96abcc71937865ac11823f09c26015db20b3553e93f076271","compact":"91e7aae3d2266bb0bd2db01a859225411a14c929ec403fe563b28d3860ef781b","nasal":"8864093ce7448ce76f68ee7c600c7b79a6cf00ab7bb0d03fd0671ec275cff514"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-42-13","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":42,"verse":13,"english":"He severed the Sāla by means of four shafts, and wounded the monkey in the arm with five, in the chest, with one, and with ten, between the teast.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.871,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-44-12"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5042013","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"5025b54c051882a5069976d27a345510c6efde628f3944afca74c5a89a1d509b","compact":"b3a4a3b6d90fb41a1971f26dc182e2c27c214dfefac5c8683fea167841c6d230","nasal":"6e757dd0b1a97429bb7f63344cf4f24b39260fc66b3059798560f2a0c5117649"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-42-14","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":42,"verse":14,"english":"With his body covered all over with shafts, (Hanumān) getting into a furious passion, taking up the same bolt, again began to swing it with rapidity.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-44-13"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5042014","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"a44404631a5cc63a4f830ffd4e8098b2c2bcc810a5322590b35d1c25f1674499","compact":"8dc4112c0f3435b0a1e38822d5f878d99483c3f1add97dd3084a478548145333","nasal":"8dc4112c0f3435b0a1e38822d5f878d99483c3f1add97dd3084a478548145333"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-42-15","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":42,"verse":15,"english":"That terrific one gifted with exceeding impetuosity, having whirled the bolt with wondrous rapidity, let it light upon Jambumāli's spacious breast.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.696,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-44-14"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5042015","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7fc0a03fba4f44db93d78d6c80e2f527fd889f76a7fe52a0d079003cb514a344","compact":"70b40aaddf02c652431b223af6daed8756e9386180256adfe0d30fe66bb7e3eb","nasal":"843db4b6d15b47bd3f47e6043ec5b919258869e34e628f5db39e0b905cabd8d5"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-42-16","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":42,"verse":16,"english":"And (non) there was neither seen there his head, nor his arms, nor his thighs, nor his bow, nor his car, nor his steeds, nor his arrows at that place.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.746,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-44-15"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5042016","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"168ab72c8b2b5bb9548246517198710d1faaeb85ca306f994972cc5e2e06408d","compact":"22f8def9d663ff9a901c0b7d541fff8a3a3c